---A storage volume.
---@class gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.Volume
---@field emergencySizeGib? string Additional emergency size that was requested for this Volume, in GiB. current_size_gib includes this value.
---@field instances? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.StringList Output only. Instances this Volume is attached to. This field is set only in Get requests.
---@field maxSizeGib? string Maximum size volume can be expanded to in case of evergency, in GiB.
---@field labels? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.StringMap Labels as key value pairs.
---@field attached? boolean Output only. Is the Volume attached at at least one instance. This field is a lightweight counterpart of `instances` field. It is filled in List responses as well.
---@field bootVolume? boolean Output only. Whether this volume is a boot volume. A boot volume is one which contains a boot LUN.
---@field protocol? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.VolumeProtocolEnum|string Output only. Storage protocol for the Volume.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of this `Volume`. Resource names are schemeless URIs that follow the conventions in https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/resource_names. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/volumes/{volume}`
---@field originallyRequestedSizeGib? string Originally requested size, in GiB.
---@field requestedSizeGib? string The requested size of this storage volume, in GiB.
---@field performanceTier? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.VolumePerformanceTierEnum|string Immutable. Performance tier of the Volume. Default is SHARED.
---@field workloadProfile? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.VolumeWorkloadProfileEnum|string The workload profile for the volume.
---@field notes? string Input only. User-specified notes for new Volume. Used to provision Volumes that require manual intervention.
---@field state? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.VolumeStateEnum|string The state of this storage volume.
---@field id? string An identifier for the `Volume`, generated by the backend.
---@field pod? string Immutable. Pod name. Pod is an independent part of infrastructure. Volume can only be connected to the instances allocated in the same pod.
---@field autoGrownSizeGib? string The size, in GiB, that this storage volume has expanded as a result of an auto grow policy. In the absence of auto-grow, the value is 0.
---@field storageType? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.VolumeStorageTypeEnum|string The storage type for this volume.
---@field currentSizeGib? string The current size of this storage volume, in GiB, including space reserved for snapshots. This size might be different than the requested size if the storage volume has been configured with auto grow or auto shrink.
---@field expireTime? string Output only. Time after which volume will be fully deleted. It is filled only for volumes in COOLOFF state.
---@field snapshotReservationDetail? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.SnapshotReservationDetail Details about snapshot space reservation and usage on the storage volume.
---@field snapshotEnabled? boolean Whether snapshots are enabled.
---@field remainingSpaceGib? string The space remaining in the storage volume for new LUNs, in GiB, excluding space reserved for snapshots.
---@field snapshotAutoDeleteBehavior? gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.VolumeSnapshotAutoDeleteBehaviorEnum|string The behavior to use when snapshot reserved space is full.

---Configuration parameters for a new volume.
---@class gcp.baremetalsolution_v2.VolumeConfig
